---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
	title="Booking software for community pottery studios"
	description="Kilnbook helps community and membership pottery studios share kilns, let members book wheel time and run open-studio hours without the whiteboard."
>
	<section class="band-dark page-hero">
		<div class="wrap split">
			<div>
				<p class="eyebrow">For community studios</p>
				<h1>One studio, a hundred members, three kilns.</h1>
				<p class="lede">
					Community studios run on shared everything: shared wheels, shared shelves, shared kilns.
					Kilnbook keeps track of who is booked, what is firing and who owes what, so open studio
					stays open instead of turning into admin.
				</p>
				<a href="/contact" class="btn">Book a demo</a>
			</div>
			<img
				src="/images/studio-floor.svg"
				alt="A floor plan of a community studio with wheels, hand-building tables and a kiln room"
				width="560"
				height="360"
			/>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="section section-alt">
		<div class="wrap">
			<p class="eyebrow">Sound familiar?</p>
			<h2>What gets hard as a membership studio grows</h2>
			<div class="cards">
				<div class="card">
					<h3>Everyone wants Tuesday at 7pm</h3>
					<p>
						The good wheels go to whoever arrives first, members on the cheaper tier book as much as
						anyone else, and nobody knows a slot is free until they drive over.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="card">
					<h3>The kiln log is a clipboard</h3>
					<p>
						Pieces pile up on the bisque shelf with no name on them, firing fees are counted by hand
						at the end of the month, and members keep asking if their mugs are out yet.
					</p>
				</div>
				<div class="card">
					<h3>Classes and members compete for space</h3>
					<p>
						A Saturday wheel course needs eight wheels that members also want, and the waitlist
						lives in someone's inbox.
					</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="wrap section narrow">
		<h2>Wheel time that follows your membership rules</h2>
		<p>
			Members reserve wheels, hand-building tables and shared equipment in one-hour blocks from their
			phone. Set how many hours each tier gets a week, how far ahead they can book, and whether
			evenings and weekends count double. A tablet by the door handles open-studio check-in, so you
			always know who is in the building while the kilns are running.
			<a href="/features/wheel-time">How wheel and table booking works</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>Shared kilns without the clipboard</h2>
		<p>
			Members log each piece when they set it on the shelf and pay the firing fee by cubic inch or by
			piece. Every kiln gets its own bisque and glaze queues, so you can see how full each load is
			before you fire it. When a load is unloaded, everyone with work in it gets a pickup text.
			<a href="/features/firings">How firing queues work</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>Classes that share the floor with members</h2>
		<p>
			Run six-week courses, drop-ins and class packs alongside memberships. Waitlists offer cancelled
			seats by text, students get a reminder the day before, and instructors see their own roster and
			mark attendance from the studio tablet.
			<a href="/features/classes">How classes and packs work</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>Which plan fits a community studio?</h2>
		<p>
			Most community studios start on the Studio plan at $79 a month. It covers up to 3 kilns with
			unlimited members, wheel and table reservations, class packs, waitlists and memberships, and
			pickup texts. If you add a fourth kiln or a second location, Collective has no kiln limit.
			<a href="/pricing">Compare plans</a>.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="cta-band">
		<div class="wrap">
			<h2>Give your members the studio back.</h2>
			<p>30 days free on the Studio plan. No card to start, and nothing is deleted if you walk away.</p>
			<a href="/contact" class="btn btn-dark">Book a demo</a>
		</div>
	</section>
</Base>
